        <mxCell id="note1" value="&lt;b&gt;Design rationale&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. AI = workload archetype MG → strict ai-lz-guardrails inherit cleanly without touching existing Production/NonProduction workloads&lt;br&gt;2. AI MG scope = one boundary for RBAC delegation to AI team · Defender for AI plans · Cost Management view (feeds Appendix A break-even trigger)&lt;br&gt;3. Phase 2 Governance Hub is a shared platform service → AI-Platform sits beside Connectivity/Identity under Platform; nothing created until triggers fire&lt;br&gt;4. Subscription strategy: Phase 1 = AI-Production + AI-NonProduction with RG-per-project; at scale = subscription vending per project, mapping 1:1 to Citadel Access Contracts&lt;br&gt;5. Multi-subsidiary: pattern repeats (Subsidiary-N &gt; AI); definitions stay at tenant root, assignments per AI MG" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#D5E2EB;fontColor=#3A3F47;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;arcSize=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="80" y="640" width="1235" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
